==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Good option for beginners.
* Low price.
* Low mastery requirements.
* Particularly useful for new players who do not have a [[Blox Fruit]].
* Both moves have [[AoE]].

|'''[Z] Quiet Rush'''
* Quick start.

|'''[X] Air Slash'''
* Decent damage.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* Does not [[Instinct Break|break Instinct]].
* Very low damage output.
* The cooldowns are very long for such a weak weapon, making it very ineffective, especially at such a low point in the game.
* For its stage in the game, the Katana's upgrade cost is exorbitant due to the requirement of [[Angel Wings]], a [[Materials|material]] that can only be dropped by enemies in [[Upper Skylands]], which are Lv. 450+.

|'''[Z] Quiet Rush'''
* Bad range.

|'''[X] Air Slash'''
* Easy to dodge due to its small range and slow speed.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* The Katana used to have a price of {{Money|5,000}} instead of {{Money|1,000}}.
* The Katana is functionally identical to the [[Cutlass]], sharing the same moveset, damage values, and cooldowns even though granted, they are different [[swords]]. The only distinction between the two weapons is their model design.
* The Katana and [[Cutlass]] are the first obtainable swords a normal player can get.

